  "marketSentiment": "NEUTRAL_BULLISH",
  "macroTheme": "Massive NFP miss (+29K vs ~90K expected) collapses October Fed hike odds to ~20%, sending Nasdaq to a record close. But the 10Y yield holds at 5.28% and gold continues its correction from 5,586 ATH. AI concentration drives the rally while Dow, small-caps, and commodities struggle.",
  "macroOverview": "The September jobs report was a bombshell that flipped the market narrative: payrolls +29K against ~90K expected, unemployment 4.2%, prior months revised down 60K. October hike odds collapsed from ~60% to ~20%. The 'bad news is good news' dynamic sent the Nasdaq to a record 30,807.93 while the Dow fell 1.26% on the week. The 10Y Treasury yield hit 5.34% Thursday before retreating to 5.28% on the NFP print. Gold sold off despite rate relief -- a deeply bearish signal. WTI crude eased to $91.11 on a G7 emergency reserve release. Treasury auctions ($119B total Tue-Thu), FOMC minutes Wednesday, and ISM Services Monday are the immediate catalysts. The midterm elections on November 3 loom as the next major risk event.",
